  "conclusion": "Not suitable for training a demand-forecast, shortage or route-disruption model. There is no calendar year/date, no SKU/item identifier and no location identifier, so no time series can be formed. Every numeric column is consistent with an independent uniform draw over a fixed range (Quantity Sold is integer-valued, 450-599), the largest absolute pairwise correlation is about 0.01, no month effect survives a multiple-comparison correction (temperature has no seasonal cycle), and route distance is not stable within a route ID. These properties are typical of randomly generated tabular data and give no evidence of real-world provenance; the file documents no source or licence. It is therefore used only for schema validation/profiling, never for training or for any displayed metric.",
